{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244670",
      "title": "The useCallback Hook",
      "sourceHash": "be1ee39f06e6122d2be8b8e5c83036fef78e4d8f7817056f1dde1612c20d85cb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 2.22,
          "en": "So in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.35,
          "en": "I explained why we can face",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.35,
          "end": 7.47,
          "en": "an infinite loop when adding functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.47,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "as dependencies to useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "It's a real problem, which I explained",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 15.42,
          "en": "in great detail in that previous lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.42,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "Now, thankfully though, the fix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "for this problem is straightforward and simple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 25.77,
          "en": "because React offers a hook which you can use to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.77,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "that this function is not recreated all the time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 31.83,
          "en": "and you should use that special hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.83,
          "end": 34.969,
          "en": "to fix this potential problem here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.969,
          "end": 36.84,
          "en": "Now, this special hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.84,
          "end": 40.246,
          "en": "which you can use is the useCallback Hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.246,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "another hook offered by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.11,
          "en": "And the idea behind this hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.11,
          "end": 49.11,
          "en": "is that you wrap it around a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.11,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "around this handleRemovePlace function in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 56.88,
          "en": "For this, you execute, useCallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.88,
          "end": 59.73,
          "en": "and then you pass the function that should be wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.73,
          "end": 63.003,
          "en": "as a first argument to useCallback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 67.86,
          "en": "Then useCallback also takes a second argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.86,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "which should be an array of dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 74.84,
          "en": "a concept that might sound familiar from useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 74.84,
          "end": 78.57,
          "en": "I'll get back to this array in just a second",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.57,
          "end": 82.5,
          "en": "because useCallback also does something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.5,
          "end": 87.33,
          "en": "It returns a value, specifically, it returns that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.33,
          "end": 92.07,
          "en": "which you wrapped, but now such that it's not recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.07,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "whenever this surrounding component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 96.87299999999999,
          "en": "is executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.87299999999999,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "So with useCallback, React makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 103.5,
          "en": "that this inner-function is not recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.5,
          "end": 106.74000000000001,
          "en": "Instead, it stores it internally in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.74000000000001,
          "end": 109.22999999999999,
          "en": "and reuses that stored function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.22999999999999,
          "end": 112.35,
          "en": "whenever the component function executes again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.35,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "So now this is not recreated, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 118.92,
          "en": "if we save this now and I reload and wait",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.92,
          "end": 123.27,
          "en": "for this all to load, add an element and open this modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.27,
          "end": 127.59,
          "en": "Now you see the timer is set, but it's then not set again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.59,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "The modal doesn't disappear because I haven't fixed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "this code yet, but we don't have this infinite loop anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 139.41,
          "en": "and that's why you should useCallback when passing functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.41,
          "end": 141.543,
          "en": "as dependencies to useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 147,
          "en": "But speaking of dependencies, useCallback actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147,
          "end": 150.51,
          "en": "also takes a dependency array here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 150.51,
          "end": 153.99,
          "en": "and this dependency array indeed works exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 153.99,
          "end": 156.72,
          "en": "as the dependency array of useEffect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 156.72,
          "end": 160.957,
          "en": "Here, you should add any prop or state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 160.957,
          "end": 164.523,
          "en": "that are used inside of this wrapped function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 166.96800000000002,
          "en": "And in this case, I got none.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 166.96800000000002,
          "end": 170.534,
          "en": "I'm using a state updating function, which does not have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.534,
          "end": 174.42000000000002,
          "en": "to be added, and I'm using some browser features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 175.65,
          "en": "like local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 175.65,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "or this JSON object, which also don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 182.11,
          "en": "to be added because they don't trigger this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.11,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "to be rendered again or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 188.193,
          "en": "It's prop or state values that should be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 193.71,
          "en": "So therefore here, having an empty array is fine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.71,
          "end": 195.87,
          "en": "and just as with useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.87,
          "end": 199.32,
          "en": "React will now only recreate this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 202.74,
          "en": "with useCallback if your dependencies changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.74,
          "end": 205.23,
          "en": "But if you have an empty array of dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.23,
          "end": 207.36,
          "en": "there is nothing that could change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207.36,
          "end": 210.625,
          "en": "and therefore, this function isn't recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.625,
          "end": 213.54399999999998,
          "en": "And with that, I'll now comment back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.54399999999998,
          "end": 218.54399999999998,
          "en": "in that setModalIsOpen call so that the modal is removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.7,
          "end": 221.31,
          "en": "But I'll also keep useCallback",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.31,
          "end": 224.25,
          "en": "because this gives us the extra safety",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 224.25,
          "end": 226.893,
          "en": "that we won't face this infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}